PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
A comprehensive evaluation of the experimental data and pharmacological principles confirms that all positive answer choices (A, B, D, E, F, G, H, and I) contain critical factual or methodological flaws. The ADC demonstrated superior anti-inflammatory potency compared to anti-TNF alone, ruling out A, while GRM monotherapy effectively reduced inflammation, ruling out G. Bone loss measurements differed markedly between anti-TNF and ADC cohorts (-0.75 mm³ versus -0.3 mm³), disproving identical osteoporosis risk in B, D, and H. Because the small-molecule GRM payload comprises only a tiny fraction of the antibody conjugate's mass, equal mass dosing neither reflects equimolar payload exposure nor reduces free steroid toxicity, refuting E, F, and I. Consequently, consensus firmly establishes that C ("None of the above is correct") is the only valid answer.
}

